      "sample_index": 0,
      "text": "We can think of arranging 9 people in a straight line with no restrictions. There are 9! ways to do this.\n\nHowever, since it is a round table, someone can be considered the same if it is a rotation of the same arrangement. For a circular arrangement, we would initially count these as $9!$ distinct arrangements. But recognize that each unique circular arrangement is equivalent to $9$ different linear rotations.\n\nTo account for these rotations, we need to divide the total by $9$. Hence, we get the final answer as $\\frac{9!}{9}=8!=\\boxed{40320}$. The answer is:\n40320",
